nts":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T02:15:22-07:00","id":1524087,"title":"","content":"As a Hungarian, I find it <i>very</i> distasteful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T09:23:11-07:00","id":1524103,"title":"","content":"Why would Hungarian fascists blow up three city blocks in Vienna of all places? I approve of fascism featuring in VtM, but it either needs to be realistic or have enough context to be established as an alternate fantasy, like Norsefire in <i>V for Vendetta</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T10:18:50-07:00","id":1524104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523869-v5-united-nations-vienna-recovery-zone?p=1524103#post1524103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Hungarian fascists blow up three city blocks in Vienna of all places? I approve of fascism featuring in VtM, but it either needs to be realistic or have enough context to be established as an alternate fantasy, like Norsefire in <i>V for Vendetta</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the veil out. What the Second Inquisition claimed was responsible for the incident. Why the authors picked them, I got no idea. I still find the whole scenario improbable. The bombing of the city center of Vienna with drones from Rammstein would have seriously changed the geopolitical image of the EU. Considering that Austria is not a part of the same arms treaties as Germany or Hungary, the implications of this would be pretty insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T10:34:50-07:00","id":1524105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523869-v5-united-nations-vienna-recovery-zone?p=1524086#post1524086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> this is probably a snarky referance to Hungarian politics were the government is far right to the point of facism. If so they really should know better after the last few incidents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very likely why it's Hungary. But it's the same sort of poorly researched writing that also gave us that bit in Second Inquisition about a persecuted religious minority-group supposedly allying themselves with the Christian fundamentalist Second Inquisition. Even if one thinks the political situation in Hungary is bad, you're still not even close to explaining how and why fascists from that country ended up destroying a couple of blocks in Vienna.<br /> <br /> Not only is WOD5E trying to turn away from lore/worldbuilding in general when it comes to the supernatural side of things but when the real-world-history is implicated in the vague worldbuilding that's left, you get bad writing like this. And it's bad writing because there's an obvious &quot;vague explanation&quot;: It was deemed a terrorist attack - even though there has been no terrorist-organization that has officially claimed credit for it. And then some line about how that contradiction has spawned a lot of conspiracy-theories. Easy peasy. Terrorism and conspiracy-theories are two hot-button-issues that can be utilized in a game. &quot;Hungarian fascists&quot;, though...? That's strangely highly specific and it's not like the rest of the book is any help in bringing that tidbit into a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T19:46:34-07:00","id":1524174,"title":"","content":"On a tangent, is the book <i>Blood Sigils</i> worthwhile for someone whose primary interest is the Tzimisce perspective on sorcery, or is it all-Tremere-and-Thinbloods-all-the-time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T22:19:18-07:00","id":1524183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523869-v5-united-nations-vienna-recovery-zone?p=1524174#post1524174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a tangent, is the book <i>Blood Sigils</i> worthwhile for someone whose primary interest is the Tzimisce perspective on sorcery, or is it all-Tremere-and-Thinbloods-all-the-time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes It Is, It delves into both Koldun and Dur an Ki variants of Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Koldunism as a Blood Sorcery variante has a single Power that attunes you to an elementi of choice, and which replaces a Blood Sorcery dot. You can take multiple times to master other elements, and scry and perceive things through It.<br /> <br /> Then you have a good chunk of Koldun rituals proper, as well as Ritual creation guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T18:12:03-07:00","id":1524208,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that sounds very interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}